  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` in `src/cli/truncate.ts`, with tests in `test/cli/truncate.test.ts`, and committed both as `862f6dc`. The new tests pass (5 of 5), and `tsc --noEmit` and `biome check` report no problems. I didn't run the full `npm test` or `npm run gate`.\n\n- **Normal case:** text longer than `max` becomes the start, a `…` and the end, and the result is never longer than `max`. When the kept characters can't split evenly, the start gets the extra one. For example, `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 6)` gives `abc…ij`.\n- **Short text:** text that already fits is returned unchanged.\n- **Tiny limits:** `max` of 0 or less gives an empty string, and `max` of 1 gives just `…`.\n- **Emoji:** the function counts and cuts by code point, so it won't split a surrogate pair such as an emoji.\n\nI left the branch as `main` and didn't push or open a PR.",
